    "details": "<p>BlockHunt '26 is a beginner friendly, escalating blockchain puzzle hunt where teams sort a broken chain, mine blocks against a live difficulty target, catch a tampered chain, crack a smart contract puzzle, and close with a laptop based consensus finale.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Format:</strong> 5 stages across approximately 3 hours, testing hashing, mining, tamper evidence, smart contracts, and consensus concepts hands on.</li>\n<li><strong>Eligibility:</strong> Open to all college students. No prior blockchain knowledge required; the event is designed to be accessible for beginners while still challenging for experienced participants.</li>\n<li><strong>Team size:</strong> 2 to 3 members per team. No restriction on inter-college or inter-specialization teams.</li>\n<li><strong>Rounds:</strong> 5 main stages (1 optional bonus stage), each stage must be cleared to advance, except the optional Stage 4.</li>\n<li><strong>Duration:</strong> Approximately 3 hours total, including registration and prize distribution.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rules:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>AI assistants are permitted for general reference, but every stage requires live, human interaction with the event platform.</li>\n<li>Sharing data or answers between teams is prohibited and will lead to disqualification.</li>\n<li>Judges' and volunteers' decisions are final.</li>\n</ul>",
